          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "It keeps bouncing, each time rising back to ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\dfrac{2}{3}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " of its previous height. What is the total distance through which the weight travels?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$300\\text{ cm}$",
      "worked": "The weight first drops $60\\text{ cm}$ and rises $\\frac23\\times60=40\\text{ cm}$. Group each downward journey with the upward journey immediately following it. The first pair has distance $60+40=100\\text{ cm}$, and successive pair distances form a GP with $a=100$ and $r=\\frac23$.\n\nSince $\\left|\\frac23\\right|<1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}S_\\infty&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\&=\\frac{100}{1-\\frac23}\\\\&=300\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
